    "updated_at": "2026-11-21T15:41:37Z",
    "body": "I ran into this bug myself.\n\n> This is only for non-intercepted fragment navigations, right? With intercepted navigations, it makes sense that `stop` and `open` would abort the async interception state. But when it's not intercepted, everything is synchronous anyway. Am I missing somtehing?\n\n@noamr not just that, I think what you're missing is that navigate listeners run after the URL checks but before the URL is updated, so it isn't fully synchronous, and can hit that too.",
