    "updated_at": "2026-11-26T10:10:17Z",
    "body": "I think the proposed fix for both document.open and window.stop would be best, maybe something like:\n\n```\nIf document's node navigable is non-null:\n    If document's node navigable's ongoing navigation is a navigation ID, then stop loading document's node navigable.\n    Otherwise:\n        Let navigation be document's node navigable's active window's navigation API.\n        If navigation's ongoing navigate event is non-null, and its navigationType is not \"traverse\", then abort the ongoing navigation given navigation.\n```\n\nBut I may be missing cases",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
